1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,198
Your phone rings.

2
00:00:01,248 --> 00:00:04,274
It's your brother, scared, begging for money.

3
00:00:04,324 --> 00:00:06,102
It sounds exactly like him.

4
00:00:06,152 --> 00:00:07,319
But it's a clone.

5
00:00:07,369 --> 00:00:10,177
Priya posts videos online like all of us.

6
00:00:10,227 --> 00:00:13,190
Scammers need just a few seconds of her voice.

7
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:17,273
One security firm says under ten seconds, one column says three.

8
00:00:17,323 --> 00:00:21,402
In Indore, a teacher heard her brother's voice asking for hospital money.

9
00:00:21,452 --> 00:00:24,413
She paid ninety-seven thousand five hundred rupees.

10
00:00:24,463 --> 00:00:26,516
Was it really him, Muja?

11
00:00:26,566 --> 00:00:27,160
No.

12
00:00:27,210 --> 00:00:29,047
Her real brother never called.

13
00:00:29,097 --> 00:00:31,259
A telephone, Muja?

14
00:00:31,309 --> 00:00:38,246
Fun fact: the first phone call, in eighteen seventy-six, was Alexander Graham Bell saying, Mister Watson, come here.

15
00:00:38,296 --> 00:00:39,313
Okay...

16
00:00:39,363 --> 00:00:40,800
back to our story.

17
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:43,625
Flat tone and odd pauses are warning signs.

18
00:00:43,675 --> 00:00:48,054
But at eleven at night, with a frightened voice, nobody listens that closely.

19
00:00:48,104 --> 00:00:49,741
So set rules first.

20
00:00:49,791 --> 00:00:51,417
Pick a family safe word.

21
00:00:51,467 --> 00:00:54,127
Hang up and call back on the number you already have.

22
00:00:54,177 --> 00:00:56,572
And send no money until you've checked.

23
00:00:56,622 --> 00:00:59,555
My take: trust the process, not the voice.

24
00:00:59,605 --> 00:01:01,977
Set a safe word with your parents this week.

25
00:01:02,027 --> 00:01:04,050
The full guide is on my blog.
